<title>SOUTH KOREA: Dong Ah shrs rise on Libya deal news.</title>
<headline>Dong Ah shrs rise on Libya deal news.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Dong Ah Construction Industrial Co rose 600 won to 22,800 in early trading on Tuesday on news that the company was assured by the Libyan government of a $5.1 billion construction deal, brokers said.  </p>
<p>Dong Ah said on Monday the Libyan government has issued a letter of intent saying the third phase of the country's Great Man-made River project would be awarded to Dong Ah.</p>
<p>Dong Ah has already participated in the first two phases of the project, together worth $10.2 billion, a company statement said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
